I still play 1.4f on a regular basis. It runs as well on XP as it
was running on DOS. (There are some conditions leading to crashes,
like genociding may conflict with monster creation,...) Apart from
this, 1.4f was/is joy to play.

You may get it here:

  ftp://ftp.sunet.se/pub/games/nethack/Msdos/NH_older

Since you need an ANSI driver, anyway, I suggest you to also look at 
this website:

  http://www.kegel.com/nansi

The, IMHO, most convenient version is NNansi.com, because it doesn't
need explicit device loading:

  http://www.kegel.com/nansi/nnansi3.3/nnans193.zip

Copy NNansi.com in the directory where you "installed" Hack.exe and
create a RunNH.bat file containing these two lines:

nnansi
hack

Adjust Hack.cnf to your needs (as always...). The following should
do fine if you installed Nethack in a NH14 (sub-)directory:

HACKDIR=..\NH14
LEVELS=..\NH14
SAVE=..\NH14;n
OPTIONS=silent,rawio,IBMBIOS,!pickup
OPTIONS=name:XYZ
GRAPHICS = 179 196 218 191 192 217 206 46 176

After you started the program with above created RunNH.bat, you may 
press <Alt>+<Enter> to play full screen. (Hit the same combination, 
again, to reactivate Window mode.)

Btw., if you like playing these old versions, you also should have a
look at Donnie Russel's revival pages (ClassicRogue, TileRogue, and
RevivedHack):

  http://www.freewebs.com/drussell/index.htm

They are all fun to play. And, AFAICT, more stable than the original
versions were...  ;-)

